WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.257
Here is how it works.

00:00:01.337 --> 00:00:06.671
Robust training minimises the usual mean-squared
error plus lambda times a penalty on

00:00:06.751 --> 00:00:09.600
the network's Jacobian at each training point.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.803
To handle the joint object, the network and its
Jacobian together,

00:00:13.883 --> 00:00:19.726
the authors recast the convergence question as a
tensor program and apply the Master theorem.

00:00:19.806 --> 00:00:26.667
They then define the finite JNTK from the
parameter-gradients of both the output and each Jacobian component.

00:00:26.747 --> 00:00:31.125
The crucial step is showing this kernel does not
move during training;

00:00:31.205 --> 00:00:35.519
that turns the learning dynamics into a linear
differential equation,

00:00:35.599 --> 00:00:40.487
and its infinite-time solution is a kernel
regression using the limiting JNTK,

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:45.900
rescaled by a simple diagonal matrix that carries
the regularisation strength lambda.
